A||||7||Matt86Z||New guy here, Hello! and a couple questions...||||2||
Z||000000||Matt86Z||06-10-2001||07:58 PM||||Hey all, I'm from eastern Canada, and I just registered. <P>I've been a closet fiero lover, always checking out GT's as they go by. I own a Z/28, as my name suggests, but I'm looking at getting a car I can drive all year round. <P>I know fieros can handle well, and my Z is no slouch in the twisties, but I'm wondering wether I should just keep my car and buy a POS toyota for the winter, or get the 86GT I've liked for a while and get a bike too!<P>Anybody come from my side to yours? any advice on what to look for? What to look out for?<P>Thanks for having me!||||reg||2
Z||000001||Cheever2||06-10-2001||08:47 PM||||Well, you've been waiting an hour, so I'll reply just to say Welcome.  <P>Although I cringe at the thought of a Fiero being exposed to cold & snow, I have the luxury of avoiding it year round, and many simply have no other transportation in the winter.  If you have the choice, I would hope you don't submit one of the diminishing numbers of Fieros to those elements, but reality tells me if you don't, someone else will.  Do what you have to do, we won't be upset about it.<P>Several camaro owners are among our ranks, but are not vocal about it here, simply because this is a Fiero forum.<P>Good to have you.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||88CoupeV6||06-11-2001||11:42 AM||||Welcome to the forum  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Josh <B>(known by TheFiero64 for first 1239 posts)</B><BR>     <IMG SRC="http://people.ne.mediaone.net/fiero64/Fiero642.jpg">    <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||7
Z||000003||Toddster||06-11-2001||11:53 AM||||If you have the choice, by an 88GT or Formula. Once you drive an 88, you can't go back!||||reg||1
Z||000004||Galen||06-11-2001||12:53 PM||||How can you say that Toddster? Any fiero, with the right amount of work can handle as good or better than a 88. If I had my choice, I'd keep my 88. But its not right to not keep an open mind about all year fieros.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> just my opinion.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.webjolt.f2s.com/pictures/galen-sig2.gif">    <BR><A HREF="http://www.webjolt.f2s.com/" TARGET=_blank>WebJolt Pictures</A> - 1988 Hawaiin Orchid Coupe w/ sunroof<BR><A HREF="http://aim:goim?screenname=GalenRPG&message=Hi!" TARGET=_blank>AIM: GalenRPG</A>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Pontiaddict||06-11-2001||10:37 PM||||Welcome, I used to have an 86 Trans Am before I got my 86 GT. There is a big differance in the feel of Fieros and F-bodies. It takes a little while to get used to not having a v8 too. Unless you out one back in.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> As far as your decision, pick the one that you feel is going to be the best deal. <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.webjolt.f2s.com/pictures/ponaddict.gif">  <BR>"The most successful American mid-engine car ever built"||||reg||1
Z||000006||Fformula88||06-11-2001||11:04 PM||||Welcome to the Forum!  Fieros actually make decent winter cars.  They are no 4x4 of course, but as long as there isn't really deep snow on the road the Fiero will get you thru.  My father has driven a Fiero year round since 1990 in Buffalo (Tons of snow!) and never gotten stuck.  The plastic body is perfect because it won't rust and make your car look ugly.  Un fortunately the body (esp. floorboards) will eventually rust out, but it will take a LOT of winters to do this.  Try and find a Fiero that is relatively rust free underneath and you will have years of happy motoring!<P>------------------<BR>John  <BR>AOLIM: Fformula88<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fierosig2.JPG"> <BR>1988 Fiero Formula<BR>1985 Fiero SE 2M6||||reg||1
Z||000007||Smoooooth GT||06-11-2001||11:53 PM||||Welcome to the forum...  Only you can make the best decision for your situation...<BR>I also avoid the snow here in Texas... well..  a few times in the last 20 year's.. only on the ground for a day or two..<BR>But ..If you do get a Fiero, This Forum is the BEST FIERO FORUM on the web,hand's down!!<BR>Great Idea's for engine upgrades, interior,body modification's...  Steve<P>------------------<BR>aka..FieroSEt<BR>Fiero_87GT@yahoo.com<BR>cell.. 903 445 0849<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_6.JPG"> ||||reg||6
